# Git & PR conventions

- Branch names: `agent/<ticket-id>-<slug>` for agent work,
  `feat|fix|chore/<ticket-id>-<slug>` for human work.
- Conventional Commits: `feat(scope): ...`, `fix(scope): ...`, etc.
  Reference the ticket: `feat(auth): add session refresh (GH-123)`.
- One logical change per PR. Stacked PRs over mega-PRs.
- Every PR description must contain these sections:
  ## What & why  (link the spec)
  ## How it was tested  (paste actual test output)
  ## Spec deviations  ("None" or an explanation)
  ## Security findings  ("None" or details)
- Never force-push shared branches. Never commit directly to main (sole
  exception: bootstrap-project on a zero-commit repo, see AGENTS.md).
  Non-ticket work uses `agent/repo-<slug>` (see AGENTS.md § Non-ticket work).
